-- saltstraumen-coalfish: Miljodirektoratet Naturbase plan register (fpnv.naturbase.no, VV00003081) read twice via WebFetch with verbatim quotes: management plan approved 10.02.2025, revision planned 2035; "Det er et intensivt sportsfiske, spesielt i selve Saltstraumen"; divers cleared 705 kg of lost lures in 2024 (about 23,500 lures at an assumed 30 g); the manager will arrange annual diver clean-ups. Lovdata protection regulation (FOR-2013-06-21-694) par.4 exempts fishing under the salmon and inland fish act and marine-resource harvesting (not kelp/seaweed). No parking or ramp detail included: the only parking source found was a non-official hiking site. Earlier skip note superseded.
--
-- gaula-river-salmon: Miljodirektoratet page "Betale fiskeravgift for laksefiske", read via WebFetch (Norwegian): anyone over 18 fishing salmon, sea trout or sea char in a watercourse must pay the state fiskeravgift; under-18s are exempt from the fee; fiskeravgift is separate from the local fiskekort, which is bought from the landowner or river administrator. Advisory-style record: the river-specific rules for the Gaula (season dates, catch reporting, release rules) are published by river-owner associations, not an official page, so none are restated. Statsforvalteren i Trondelag pages that would cover them returned 404 via WebFetch. Fine amount deliberately omitted.
--
-- namsen-river-salmon: Miljodirektoratet page "Betale fiskeravgift for laksefiske", read via WebFetch (Norwegian): anyone over 18 fishing salmon, sea trout or sea char in a watercourse must pay the state fiskeravgift; under-18s are exempt from the fee; fiskeravgift is separate from the local fiskekort, which is bought from the landowner or river administrator. Advisory-style record: the river-specific rules for the Namsen (season dates, catch reporting, release rules) are published by river-owner associations, not an official page, so none are restated. Statsforvalteren i Trondelag pages that would cover them returned 404 via WebFetch. Fine amount deliberately omitted.
--
-- femunden-grayling: Statskog page "Femundsmarka" (state land manager) read via WebFetch (Norwegian), plus Engerdal Fjellstyre page "Hvordan kjope fiskekort" (statutory mountain board): a shared Femundsmarka card covers all waters inside the national park in Engerdal and Roros and is sold online (inatur.no) and by SMS; species listed are char, whitefish, perch, pike, burbot, and trout and grayling in the rivers; Statskog states fishing is free under 20 and over 67; entry points named are Feragen, Feragsdammen, Langen and the Faemund 2 shuttle boat from Synnervika to Roa; Statskog rents cabins at Synnervika, Feragsdambua, Hestbetaasbua and Nordviksanden. Engerdal Fjellstyre says permits are now sold digitally only and that the park card is valid only inside the park boundary; outside it the ordinary Engerdal permit applies. No parking detail stated on either page, so none given. No prices stated.
--
-- senja-halibut: Fiskeridirektoratet (Directorate of Fisheries) page "Freda og delvis freda artar" under Fritidsfiske, read via WebFetch with verbatim quotes: halibut fishing is forbidden year-round south of Stad (62N), and north of Stad from 20 December to 20 April, for all gear. Senja (about 69N) is north of Stad. The page carries no update date and a 2026 halibut regulation consultation exists on the same site, so the record states the closed period with a check-current-rules pointer. Bag/gear/hook numbers and the tourist export allowance were seen in search summaries and deliberately left out (rule 3). No access or ramp page found; this is a regulation-only record.
--
-- nagara-river-ayu: Gifu Prefecture official page "Gifu-ken no gyogyoken" (pref.gifu.lg.jp/page/11131.html), read via WebFetch (Japanese): on Type 5 common fishing-right waters, recreational anglers need the permission of the fishing cooperative that holds the right, and each area has its own recreational fishing rules (yuryo kisoku); the Nagara River is split among several cooperatives (Kiso-Nagara Lower River, Nagara River, Nagara River Central, Gujo, Tsubo River, Miyama, Itatori Upper River); the page states the current rights run 1 Jan 2026 to 31 Dec 2035. The page does not name the permit or give fees or seasons, so none are stated (fees and seasons appeared only on a cooperative site and search summaries). Previous skip note superseded.
--
-- rio-sao-francisco: IEF-MG (Instituto Estadual de Florestas, Minas Gerais state forestry institute) page "Piracema", read via WebFetch with verbatim quotes (Portuguese): the piracema/defeso runs from 1 November to 28 February of the following year; fishing is prohibited, amateur fishing is allowed only for non-native (exotic/alochthonous) species and hybrids, native fish caught accidentally must be released, and anglers must hold a current amateur fishing licence (types A1 shore, A2 boat, A3 underwater); the page points to Portaria IEF 154/2011 for the Sao Francisco basin. Applies to the Minas Gerais side only: the Bahia side is under Bahia rules, not read, so the record says so. Ibama and MMA pages on the same topic returned "Conteudo Restrito" via WebFetch. Existing regulations said the closure was "roughly" Nov-Feb; this gives the stated dates.
--
-- campeche-tarpon: CONAPESCA (Mexican federal fisheries commission) procedure page CONAPESCA-01-016 "Permiso para Pesca Deportivo-Recreativa", read via WebFetch with verbatim quotes (Spanish): the permit is available to Mexican and foreign individuals; fishing from land "no requerira de permiso"; fishing aboard a vessel requires the permits under the Ley Federal de Derechos; permit types are daily, weekly, monthly, annual and excursion, obtained at CONAPESCA offices or online (e5cinco). National rule, not specific to Campeche; no spot-specific official page found, so the record is deliberately limited to the permit rule and carries no ramp, parking or facility claims. Fees omitted.
--
-- lake-el-salto-bass: CONAPESCA (Mexican federal fisheries commission) procedure page CONAPESCA-01-016 "Permiso para Pesca Deportivo-Recreativa", read via WebFetch with verbatim quotes (Spanish): the permit is available to Mexican and foreign individuals; fishing from land "no requerira de permiso"; fishing aboard a vessel requires the permits under the Ley Federal de Derechos; permit types are daily, weekly, monthly, annual and excursion, obtained at CONAPESCA offices or online (e5cinco). National rule, not specific to Lake El Salto; no spot-specific official page found, so the record is deliberately limited to the permit rule and carries no ramp, parking or facility claims. Fees omitted.
--
-- lake-baccarac-bass: CONAPESCA (Mexican federal fisheries commission) procedure page CONAPESCA-01-016 "Permiso para Pesca Deportivo-Recreativa", read via WebFetch with verbatim quotes (Spanish): the permit is available to Mexican and foreign individuals; fishing from land "no requerira de permiso"; fishing aboard a vessel requires the permits under the Ley Federal de Derechos; permit types are daily, weekly, monthly, annual and excursion, obtained at CONAPESCA offices or online (e5cinco). National rule, not specific to Lake Baccarac; no spot-specific official page found, so the record is deliberately limited to the permit rule and carries no ramp, parking or facility claims. Fees omitted.
